{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2443 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "867eebc2fdebb014bec28c3fe1b8cea24e2a9fcabba4401fe0cf18abacaef0fc" :edb/db-before-t 2442 :edb/db-after-t 2443 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535755 50 #inst "2026-10-09T06:36:54.395Z" 13194139535755 true] [17592186147437 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364876 13194139535755 true] [17592186147438 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364869 13194139535755 true] [17592186147439 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364890 13194139535755 true] [17592186147440 1020 #edb/ref 17592186364883 13194139535755 true] [17592186148070 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535755 true] [17592186148070 1100 "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n2xy\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" 13194139535755 true] [17592186148070 1100 "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$2xydx + (x^{2} - y^{2})dy = 0$." 13194139535755 false] [17592186148070 1145 "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=2xy$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int 2xy\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=0,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}=c.\n$$" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364869 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364870 13194139535755 true] [17592186364869 1089 "q-103178" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364869 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535755 true] [17592186364869 1100 "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\n- $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y$\n- $xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$\n- $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364869 1113 #uuid "8e4d2f85-2640-5963-a9fc-d023ea35768b" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364869 1145 "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-1\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$  gives an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''III only''." 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364871 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364872 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364873 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364874 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364875 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1041 "selection" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364871 13194139535755 true] [17592186364870 1110 #uuid "63ec2927-e81a-52bb-9f83-5e274ada1c1a" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364871 1034 "ÍII only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364871 1111 #uuid "83a84f38-7fa4-5f35-9267-38cccc0737c1" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364872 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364872 1111 #uuid "7a1c6496-69fd-543b-861c-74f379755198" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364873 1034 "I only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364873 1111 #uuid "58827855-4167-5fb9-a8a7-d621ffa996dc" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364874 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364874 1111 #uuid "2b353dae-641e-589f-90ac-887025e6d2a0" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364875 1034 "II only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364875 1111 #uuid "76493e3e-af89-548c-8e13-45db761a7433" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364876 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364877 13194139535755 true] [17592186364876 1089 "q-318629" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364876 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535755 true] [17592186364876 1100 "Which of the following differential equations is exact?  \n\n- $({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+2)\\,\\text{d}y=0$\n- $(3xy)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0$\n- $(6y-x)\\,\\text{d}y-(y-4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0$" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364876 1113 #uuid "2afce9a3-09a4-5e75-8115-6a50c9574f64" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364876 1145 "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation:\n\n- The first equation is\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+2)\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={x}^{2}+y,\\,Q(x,y)=xy+2.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+2) \\\\  & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n \nThus, equation I is not exact.\n\n- The second equation is\n\n$$\n(3xy)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=3xy,\\,Q(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3xy) \\\\  & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nThus, equation II is not exact.\n\n- The third equation is\n\n$$\n(6y-x)\\,\\text{d}y-(y-4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=-(y-4x)=4x-y,\\,Q(x,y)=6y-x.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x-y) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6y-x) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nThus, equation III is exact.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364878 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364879 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364880 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364881 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364882 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1041 "selection" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364880 13194139535755 true] [17592186364877 1110 #uuid "221e44a5-e2c8-56ec-a0d0-c6c30d4dbe67" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364878 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364878 1111 #uuid "59ade000-773d-561c-a0c0-ec271392a826" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364879 1034 "I only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364879 1111 #uuid "bfa0b0ef-eaeb-525f-97a4-19297b557408" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364880 1034 "III only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364880 1111 #uuid "65176d1a-1f86-5614-a09f-e09233b335da" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364881 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364881 1111 #uuid "a9182c8d-53b3-57a3-a556-3c4041973313" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364882 1034 "II only" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535755 true] [17592186364882 1111 #uuid "229f7401-19c6-5cf3-b967-69c635e87901" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364883 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364884 13194139535755 true] [17592186364883 1089 "q-320578" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364883 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535755 true] [17592186364883 1100 "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}}{\\,13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}\\,}.\n$$" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364883 1113 #uuid "bec2197d-40e8-5881-af2d-3978294960fc" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364883 1145 "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}}{13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y=(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x+(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4},\\,Q(x,y)={x}^{4}{y}^{3}-13y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\,(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\,4{x}^{3}{y}^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\,(x\\,(xy)^{3}-13y) \\\\  & =\\,4{x}^{3}{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n \nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =22x+\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}+f(y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{4}{y}^{3}-13y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+g(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=22x,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c.\n$$" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364885 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364886 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364887 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364888 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364889 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1041 "selection" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364889 13194139535755 true] [17592186364884 1110 #uuid "e6fcc765-0309-582c-8738-678dc78cf73f" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364885 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{x}^{2}+22x=c" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364885 1111 #uuid "26d4b2e3-5beb-558c-99c4-5caaa929a501" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364886 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22y=c" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364886 1111 #uuid "9f73d861-57aa-5a3c-a437-b2e9eb7dfc07" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364887 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}-22x=c" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364887 1111 #uuid "c10008b3-4dfb-526a-94bf-ee15e22b381b" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364888 1034 "-\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364888 1111 #uuid "2a40792e-9d57-5164-9901-cfe2bf618126" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364889 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364889 1111 #uuid "3eccf0ad-70e3-5e61-bed7-a03a26cf4e80" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364890 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364891 13194139535755 true] [17592186364890 1089 "q-64183" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364890 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535755 true] [17592186364890 1100 "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n(3{x}^{2}y-3)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(1)=0.$" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364890 1113 #uuid "3b6e7ffd-24fa-5884-897d-7e3e1edbe5ea" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364890 1145 "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y-3$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{3}+{e}^{y}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int 3{x}^{2}y-3\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}y-3x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{3}+{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}y+{e}^{y}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=-3x,\\,f(y)={e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=0$ when $x=1.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=c \\\\ (1)^{3}(0)-3(1)+{e}^{0}=c \\\\ -3+1=c \\\\ c=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=-2.\n$$" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364892 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364893 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364894 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364895 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364896 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1041 "selection" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364894 13194139535755 true] [17592186364891 1110 #uuid "1a247cc0-c26e-5066-ab1e-59b64168cdd6" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364892 1034 "{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-{e}^{x-1}+{e}^{y}=0" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364892 1111 #uuid "5101d73b-46f9-599e-8a74-002dce17a18a" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364893 1034 "{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{3}+{e}^{2y}=4" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364893 1111 #uuid "4fec5da6-9ccd-5867-ad96-dfcd96a40fa8" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364894 1034 "{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=-2" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364894 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364894 1111 #uuid "2b4cb3f4-ac37-50e1-b30c-64cf84901e51" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364895 1034 "x{y}^{3}-3x=-3" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364895 1111 #uuid "ae906e1a-0422-52f6-9eda-8c6caee10f95" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364896 1034 "{x}^{3}y-3{e}^{y}=-3" 13194139535755 true] [17592186364896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535755 true] [17592186364896 1111 #uuid "22c4c558-b05e-519b-b063-b30a32c50a21" 131941395357